4:   "summary": "No files changed. I did not run a build, because no execution tool is available, so I have not verified that the Emscripten 4.0.18 build succeeds.\n\nWhat I inspected: platform/README.md, loop/acceptance.md, and platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c. The prior coder stdout.json for build-01 was empty, so there was no earlier finding to read. Root README.md, artifacts/README.md and the build scripts are not exposed to me, so I did not read them.\n\nReview of platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c:\n- It defines every DG_* callback the engine needs.\n- It has a main() entry point that checks /doom1.wad is a valid IWAD.\n- It converts the framebuffer from B,G,R,0 to opaque RGBA.\n- It yields to the browser with emscripten_sleep, which relies on Asyncify.\n- It exports the dg_* keepalive functions used by the tests.\n- I found no apparent compile errors in this file.\n\nNot checked: platform/doom_audio.c, platform/SDL_mixer.h, web/index.html, web/audio.js, and how the engine's FEATURE_SOUND setting is handled.\n\nRemaining blockers and human-owned items:\n- The build script and its flags are human-owned and not visible to me. Someone needs to confirm they include -sASYNCIFY, --preload-file assets/doom1.wad@/doom1.wad, the exported functions, and an include path for platform/SDL_mixer.h.\n- A human or the tester must run the build with Emscripten 4.0.18 and attach its output.\n\nEvidence needed: the build log, the produced doom.js, doom.wasm and doom.data, and the tester's run of tests/test_browser.py and tests/test_audio.py tied to source digest bf73c249.",
